  "id": "kesslerfabrication",
  "neon": "#ffa04a",
  "note": "KESSLER FABRICATION — a working fabrication shed on Kessler Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: a gantry crane crawling on overhead rails, sparks fountaining from a cutting\nbench, air that tastes of ozone and hot steel; somebody in here can weld, bend or fake almost\nanything.\n\nSo the shed is a sawtooth-roofed hall with its big door open on a lit, orange interior, and the\ncrane runway carries on out of the building as an external gantry over the yard on the open side,\ntwo steel legs and a beam, which is what a fab shop that lifts things heavier than its door does.\nThe name is on the fascia over the door. A works doesn't sign itself (UNSIGNED_TRADE), and this one\nsells to the public over a counter, which is the stated exception.",
  "pal": "ty_fab_metal",
